    "result_text": "The full suite is green. There are only three test files and only `AcceptanceTest` carries `@Test` methods (the other two are support classes), so `./mvnw test` runs the whole suite \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `membershipNumber` for owners, formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` where `YY` is the last two digits of the registration date year (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`).\n\nSince the value is purely derived from the owner's own `customerCode` and `registrationDate`, I added it as a computed, read-only response field rather than a persisted column \u2014 mirroring how `displayName` and `initials` are already handled:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped `membershipNumber` via a new `formatMembershipNumber(owner)` expression:\n   ```java\n   return String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100);\n   ```\n   It returns `null` when either `customerCode` or `registrationDate` is absent, since the number can't be derived without both. The `%02d` zero-pads years like 2007 \u2192 `07`.\n\nNo entity or database changes were needed \u2014 `customerCode` is assigned on create (`saveOwner`) and `registrationDate` defaults via `@PrePersist`, so both are present by the time an owner is serialized.",
